From: Shunya Shishido <sisidovski@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:32:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M159] [ServiceWorker] Protect ServiceWorkerVersion across
 re-entrant calls

Original change's description:
> [ServiceWorker] Protect ServiceWorkerVersion across re-entrant calls
>
> When an active ServiceWorkerVersion is in kStopping after
> OnRequestTermination() called EmbeddedWorkerInstance::Stop() directly,
> no ref-holding callback is in stop_callbacks_, so
> ServiceWorkerRegistration::active_version_ can hold the last reference
> to the version. ServiceWorkerRegistration::ActivateWaitingVersion()
> then replaces active_version_ (its StopWorker() call adds no ref in
> kStopping), so the version is destroyed when activation returns.
>
> NavigateClient() calls service_worker_client_utils::NavigateClient(),
> which can reach ActivateWaitingVersion() synchronously via
> ServiceWorkerControlleeRequestHandler, and then reads `script_url_` and
> `context_` in NotifyClientNavigated(). OnNoWorkInBrowser() has the same
> problem: ServiceWorkerRegistration::OnNoWork() can activate a waiting
> version synchronously before `observers_` are iterated. OpenWindow()
> follows the same pattern as NavigateClient() with
> service_worker_client_utils::OpenWindow() and NotifyWindowOpened().
>
> Hold a scoped_refptr to `this` across these calls and add unit tests
> that drop the last reference to the version during each call.
>
